Home >> Photo Gallery >> Concrete is the material choice for public space projects because it can be installed easily, is easily maintained and adapted to many types of applications. It can serve as a construction element, decorative element or a covering that is combined with other materials such as metal or plastic in order to create unique spatial elements depending on project needs.
The concrete used is mainly for flooring projects but can also be used for the following applications :
Wall coverings (exposed concrete): the exterior wall can give the impression of being reinforced to increase durability and strength against weathering;
Exterior cladding (exposed brick): this is the exterior of the building made from wood frames coated with resin cement mixed with bitumen or other synthetic resin;
Internal cladding of industrial spaces (floor / ceilings): This is mainly characterized by the high cost of the project to achieve the visual appearance desired;

